You need to temporarily save changes without committing. How? 

1.To temporarily save our work without committing, use the git stash command.

2.git stash  takes our current changes (both staged and unstaged) and stores them on a internal stack, giving a clean working directory. 

3.To add a descriptive note, we can use git stash push -m "our message" 

4.By default, stash only tracks modified files. Use git stash -u to include untracked files. 

5.git stash pop to apply the most recent changes and immediately delete them from the stash

6.git stash apply if we want to restore the changes but keep the record in our stash for later use. 

7.git stash list to see all our temporarily saved changes. 
